Every central-nervous-system-depressant can potentiate an opioid-associated-respiratory-depression.
If a clinician prescribes an opioid with a central-nervous-system-depressant and the central-nervous-system-depressant is not a benzodiazepine then the clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk.
A central-nervous-system-depressant-example includes a muscle-relaxant-example and includes a nonbenzodiazepine-sedative-hypnotic-example and includes a potentially-sedating-anticonvulsant-example.
A potentially-sedating-anticonvulsant-example includes a gabapentin-example and includes a pregabalin-example.
